 "note": "Kookaburra Caravan Park, now the Busselton Jetty Tourist Park (Park 1), corner of Marine Tce and Brown St (2 Brown St). City of Busselton land; Category 4 on the Local Heritage Survey. From the Landgate aerial (Oct 2026), the City's 2026 park map (Reception on the Marine Tce and Brown St corner, park cabins 12, 11, 7 and 6 in the front row) and the City's cabin photos. Only what a driver sees from Marine Tce: the low-hipped reception building on the corner, four of the front-row cabins with their gable ends to the street (white Colorbond cladding, white roofs, a verandah and deck on the street end), the green bin enclosure and the path in from the footpath, and a plain lettered park sign. The rest of the park (sites, caravans, the amenities block and camp kitchen at the west end) is left to the build. Metres: x along Marine Tce, left to right as seen from it (east to west), y south from the reception's and front cabin's front walls.",
